blets recently discovered by Mr. Pinches (see CHALDEA) show the true reading is Eri-Aku of Larsa.","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1,9]},{"id":"tidal_2854","name":"Tidal","also":"","summary":"(in the LXX. called “Thorgal”), styled the “king of nations” (Gen. 14:1-9). Mentioned as Tudkhula on Arioch’s brick (see facing page 139).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1,9]},{"id":"bera_467","name":"Bera","also":"","summary":"Gift, or son of evil, king of Sodom at the time of the invasion of the four kings under Chedorlaomer (Gen. 14:2, 8, 17, 21).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"birsha_513","name":"Birsha","also":"","summary":"Son of wickedness, a king of Gomorrah whom Abraham succoured in the invasion of Chedorlaomer (Gen. 14:2).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"shemeber_2648","name":"Shemeber","also":"","summary":"Soaring on high, the king of Zeboiim, who joined with the other kings in casting off the yoke of Chedorlaomer.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"shinab_2708","name":"Shinab","also":"","summary":"Cooling, the king of Adamah, in the valley of Siddim, who with his confederates was conquered by Chedorlaomer (Gen. 14:2).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[12,13,14,19,21,22,23]},{"id":"lot_1830","name":"Lot","also":"","summary":"(Heb. goral, a “pebble”), a small stone used in casting lots (Num. 33:54; Jonah 1:7). The lot was always resorted to by the Hebrews with strictest reference to the interposition of God, and as a method of ascertaining the divine will (Prov. 16:33), and in serious cases of doubt (Esther 3:7).","verses":34,"father":"Haran","mother":"","v":[12,16]},{"id":"mamre_1923","name":"Mamre","also":"","summary":"An Amoritish chief in alliance with Abraham (Gen. 14:13, 24).","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[13,24]},{"id":"aner_266","name":"Aner","also":"","summary":"A Canaanitish chief who joined his forces with those of Abraham in pursuit of Chedorlaomer (Gen. 14:13, 24).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[13,24]},{"id":"eshcol_1218","name":"Eshcol","also":"","summary":"A young Amoritish chief who joined Abraham in the recovery of Lot from the hands of Chedorlaomer (Gen. 14:13, 24).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[13,24]},{"id":"melchisedec_1991","name":"Melchisedec","also":"Melchizedek","summary":"King of righteousness, the king of Salem. All we know of him is recorded in Gen. 14:18-20. He is subsequently mentioned only once in the Old Testament, in Ps. 110:4.","verses":11,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18]}],"places":[{"id":"elam_365","name":"Elam","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.5,"lon":49.5,"summary":"Highland, the son of Shem (Gen. 10:22), and the name of the country inhabited by his descendants (14:1, 9; Isa. 11:11; 21:2, etc.) lying to the east of Babylonia, and extending to the shore of the Mediterranean, a distance in a direct line of about 1,000 miles.","verses":14,"v":[1,9]},{"id":"ellasar_372","name":"Ellasar","kind":"Region","lat":37.05694,"lon":40.99722,"summary":"The oak or heap of Assyria, a territory in Asia of which Arioch was king (Gen. 14:1, 9). It is supposed that the old Chaldean town of Larsa was the metropolis of this kingdom, situated nearly half-way between Ur (now Mugheir) and Erech, on the left bank of the Euphrates.","verses":2,"v":[1,9]},{"id":"goiim_485","name":"Goiim","kind":"","lat":null,"lon":null,"summary":"","verses":3,"v":[1,9]},{"id":"shinar_1084","name":"Shinar","kind":"Region","lat":32.5365,"lon":44.42088,"summary":"LXX. and Vulgate “Senaar;” in the inscriptions, “Shumir;” probably identical with Babylonia or Southern Mesopotamia, extending almost to the Persian Gulf.","verses":8,"v":[1,9]},{"id":"admah_27","name":"Admah","kind":"City","lat":31.11942,"lon":35.41253,"summary":"Earth, one of the five cities of the vale of Siddim (Gen. 10:19). It was destroyed along with Sodom and Gomorrah (19:24; Deut. 29:23).","verses":5,"v":[2,8]},{"id":"bela_172","name":"Bela","kind":"City","lat":30.92652,"lon":35.41906,"summary":"A city on the shore of the Dead Sea, not far from Sodom, called also Zoar. It was the only one of the five cities that was spared at Lot’s intercession (Gen. 19:20, 23).","verses":2,"v":[2,8]},{"id":"gomorrah_489","name":"Gomorrah","kind":"City","lat":31.15725,"lon":35.47395,"summary":"Submersion, one of the five cities of the plain of Siddim which were destroyed by fire (Gen. 10:19; 13:10; 19:24, 28). These cities probably stood close together, and were near the northern extremity of what is now the Dead Sea.","verses":23,"v":[2,8,10,11]},{"id":"sodom_1107","name":"Sodom","kind":"City","lat":31.19656,"lon":35.39648,"summary":"Burning; the walled, a city in the vale of Siddim (Gen. 13:10; 14:1-16). The wickedness of its inhabitants brought down upon it fire from heaven, by which it was destroyed (18:16-33; 19:1-29; Deut. 23:17).","verses":47,"v":[2,8,10,11,12,17,21,22]},{"id":"zeboiim_1244","name":"Zeboiim","kind":"City","lat":31.11942,"lon":35.41253,"summary":"One of the “five cities of the plain” of Sodom, generally coupled with Admah (Gen. 10:19; 14:2; Deut. 29:23; Hos. 11:8). It had a king of its own (Shemeber), and was therefore a place of some importance.","verses":5,"v":[2,8]},{"id":"zoar_1271","name":"Zoar","kind":"City","lat":30.92652,"lon":35.41906,"summary":"Small, a town on the east or south-east of the Dead Sea, to which Lot and his daughters fled from Sodom (Gen. 19:22, 23). It was originally called Bela (14:2, 8).","verses":9,"v":[2,8]},{"id":"salt_sea_1021","name":"salt sea","kind":"Water","lat":31.57785,"lon":35.52394,"summary":"The name given by Greek writers of the second century to that inland sea called in Scripture the “salt sea” (Gen. 14:3; Num. 34:12), the “sea of the plain” (Deut. 3:17), the “east sea” (Ezek. 47:18; Joel 2:20), and simply “the sea” (Ezek. 47:8).","verses":9,"v":[3]},{"id":"vale_of_siddim_1218","name":"vale of Siddim","kind":"Valley","lat":31.23534,"lon":35.51762,"summary":"Valley of the broad plains, “which is the salt sea” (Gen. 14:3, 8, 10), between Engedi and the cities of the plain, at the south end of the Dead Sea.","verses":3,"v":[3,8,10]},{"id":"ashteroth-karnaim_107","name":"Ashteroth-karnaim","kind":"","lat":32.76667,"lon":36.01667,"summary":"Ashteroth of the two horns, the abode of the Rephaim (Gen. 14:5). It may be identified with Ashtaroth preceding; called “Karnaim”, i.e., the “two-horned” (the crescent moon).","verses":1,"v":[5]},{"id":"ham_514","name":"Ham","kind":"Region","lat":31.95019,"lon":35.92413,"summary":"Warm, hot, and hence the south; also an Egyptian word meaning “black”, the youngest son of Noah (Gen. 5:32; comp. 9:22, 24).","verses":1,"v":[5]},{"id":"karnaim_670","name":"Karnaim","kind":"","lat":32.76667,"lon":36.01667,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[5]},{"id":"shaveh-kiriathaim_1066","name":"Shaveh-kiriathaim","kind":"","lat":31.58333,"lon":35.7,"summary":"Plain of Kirja-thaim where Chedorlaomer defeated the Emims, the original inhabitants (Gen. 14:5).","verses":1,"v":[5]},{"id":"el-paran_376","name":"El-paran","kind":"","lat":29.15167,"lon":33.54194,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[6]},{"id":"seir_1042","name":"Seir","kind":"Region","lat":30.73469,"lon":35.60625,"summary":"The name of a mountainous region occupied by the Edomites, extending along the eastern side of the Arabah from the south-eastern extremity of the Dead Sea to near the Akabah, or the eastern branch of the Red Sea.","verses":24,"v":[6]},{"id":"en-mishpat_393","name":"En-mishpat","kind":"","lat":30.68771,"lon":34.4948,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[7]},{"id":"hazazon-tamar_542","name":"Hazazon-tamar","kind":"","lat":31.46153,"lon":35.39241,"summary":"","verses":2,"v":[7]},{"id":"kadesh_661","name":"Kadesh","kind":"Oasis","lat":30.64805,"lon":34.42261,"summary":"Holy, or Kadesh-Barnea, sacred desert of wandering, a place on the south-eastern border of Palestine, about 165 miles from Horeb. It lay in the “wilderness” or “desert of Zin” (Gen. 14:7; Num. 13:3-26; 14:29-33; 20:1; 27:14), on the border of Edom (20:16).","verses":15,"v":[7]},{"id":"dan_323","name":"Dan","kind":"Region","lat":33.24856,"lon":35.65252,"summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":20,"v":[14]},{"id":"damascus_322","name":"Damascus","kind":"City","lat":33.51161,"lon":36.3091,"summary":"Activity, the most ancient of Oriental cities; the capital of Syria (Isa. 7:8; 17:3); situated about 133 miles to the north of Jerusalem.","verses":55,"v":[15]},{"id":"hobah_571","name":"Hobah","kind":"","lat":33.5,"lon":36.46667,"summary":"Hiding-place, a place to the north of Damascus, to which Abraham pursued Chedorlaomer and his confederates (Gen. 14:15).","verses":1,"v":[15]},{"id":"valley_of_shaveh_1216","name":"valley of Shaveh","kind":"Valley","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[17]},{"id":"valley_of_shaveh_692","name":"valley of Shaveh","kind":"Valley","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"Valley of the plain the ancient name of the “king’s dale”, or Kidron, on the north side of Jerusalem (Gen. 14:17).","verses":2,"v":[17]},{"id":"salem_1018","name":"Salem","kind":"City","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"Peace, commonly supposed to be another name of Jerusalem (Gen. 14:18; Ps. 76:2; Heb. 7:1, 2).","verses":4,"v":[18]}],"events":[],"traditions":[["tithing",18,20]],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3117,3117,3117,569,4428,8152,8152,746,4428,495,495,3540,4428,5867,5867,8413,8413,4428,1471,1471],[6213,6213,4421,854,1298,4428,5467,5467,1306,4428,6017,6017,8134,4428,126,126,8038,4428,6636,6636